  (text "Used to detect if the 100v - 12V and \n12V - 5V Buck converters are working."
    (at 119.38 23.495 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid 3e648f07-1d22-424d-b126-bd5aa086183f)
  )
  (text "Schematic and Board Review comments:\n\nSchematic:\n- Delete the extra PWR_FLAG flags, those are to indicate to KiCAD that the power\n  is coming from somewhere and will suppress an error. Adding additional power flags\n  will throw another error\n\nBoard:\n- Decoupling capacitors must be placed as close to +5V of the chip as possible,\n  or it would not achieve decoupling\n- Low current 5V devices should use smaller traces, especially SMD resistors\n  and capacitors as they are prone to manufacturing defects due to uneven thermals"
    (at 88.265 185.42 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid 408def20-154b-4ef1-a7bd-6dd5ee478e9c)
  )
  (text "Arduino Nano" (at 125.095 79.375 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid 48a654ff-c897-4c43-886d-9270d29a7230)
  )
